         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/b3461431-4960-4ba4-96c2-02a2113f7277,1794506614406/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1280%2C720%29%3B' alt='On the left, a grainy photo shows a mouse running on the floor. The right shows a blue building with the word emergency above the door.' width='620' height='349' title='Documents obtained by CBC News reveal the health authority&apos;s pest control bills have soared in the last five years, including at the QEII Health Sciences Centre, where this mouse was spotted in the emergency department on Nov. 7.'/><p>CBC News has learned that several Halifax-area hospitals have been dealing with soaring costs to deal with mice and pigeon infestations. Nova Scotia Health says it could take years to rid its facilities of the mice issue.</p>]]></description>
